          },
          "create_time": 1793154188.0,
          "update_time": 1793154191.42,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I’ve read both files and saved your proposal and clarifications in the [brainstorm note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/05_radial_theta_collision_geometry/brainstorm/01_RADIAL_INTEGRAND_PRESERVING_DEFORMATIONS_AND_COLLISION_LOCALIZATION_20261027.md), with **the complete radial integrand as the sole invariant**.\n\nThe Laplacian gives a concrete starting construction. Writing \\(\\mathcal P\\) for spherical averaging,\n\\[\n\\mathcal P\\Delta=\\Delta_{\\mathrm{rad}}\\mathcal P.\n\\]\nThus a potential perturbation with \\(\\mathcal P\\Psi_s=0\\) produces\n\\[\nQ_s=Q+\\Delta\\Psi_s,\\qquad \\mathcal P Q_s=Q.\n\\]\nThe three-dimensional source changes while the radial integrand—and therefore \\(H(t,z)\\)—remains exactly fixed.\n\nThis permits localized angular perturbations, angular transport, and concentration beyond the manuscript’s Darboux family. The question becomes whether a suitable realization makes a decisive integral estimate or dynamical constraint accessible.\n\nThe discussion is recorded in [chat0007](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/05_radial_theta_collision_geometry/chat-histories/0007_2026-10-28T02-11-39Z_explore-collision-localizing-deforms.json), with capture of this final reply arranged."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
