          "create_time": 1793155286.091,
          "update_time": 1793155293.017,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I added the idea to **Sections 9–10 of the manuscript**, including explicit auxiliary flows, the transformed differential equation, and its boundary conditions. The updated 13-page PDF compiles cleanly and has been visually checked.\n\n:codex-file-citation{path=\"/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/output/pdf/radial-theta-collision-geometry/radial_deformations_and_zero_dynamics.pdf\" purpose=\"output\"}\n\nA concrete starting point is\n\\[\nA_s=\\frac{e^{sq}}{P(e^{sq})},\n\\qquad\n\\partial_sA_s=\\bigl(q-P(qA_s)\\bigr)A_s,\n\\]\nwhere \\(P\\) denotes normalized spherical averaging and \\(s\\) is an auxiliary deformation parameter. Because \\(PA_s=1\\), this preserves the complete radial integrand at every radius.\n\nChoosing the angular profile \\(q\\) using the two integrands defining \\(H\\) and \\(H_z\\) concentrates their collision cancellation near a curve in three dimensions. I derived this construction explicitly. It localizes the **representation** of the collision; the physical collision remains unchanged.\n\nThe [new brainstorm](</Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/05_radial_theta_collision_geometry/brainstorm/02_AUXILIARY_FLOWS_FOR_COLLISION_LOCALIZATION_20261027.md>) also proposes a **projected Laplacian flow** that preserves the radial integrand while decreasing a chosen localization cost. This offers a broader direction than multiplicative reweighting.\n\nThe remaining challenge is an estimate whose gain from localization exceeds the new derivative and boundary costs. The manuscript distinguishes the established finite-parameter constructions from that open contradiction argument. Supporting derivations and a self-assessment were saved, and the chat archive was refreshed with final-turn capture arranged."
            ]
          },
